# Real ballot-level preference data for the 2017 Shetland Islands Council election,
# Shetland North ward (4 candidates, 3 seats). Converted from
# https://github.com/mggg/scot-elex/blob/main/4_cands/shetland_2017_ward2.csv (MGGG's public
# archive of real Scottish STV preference profiles, described in arXiv:2605.12676).
# Cross-checked against reporting of the real result: 1192 valid votes, first preferences
# Manson 509 / Cooper 395 / Macdonald 240 / Johnson 48, and Cooper, Manson, and Macdonald
# (not Johnson) elected. Round 2/3 intermediate tallies additionally cross-checked against
# Shetland Islands Council's official "Candidate Votes Per Stage Report" for this ward
# (shetland.gov.uk, file 875): Manson and Cooper both meet quota (299) simultaneously in
# stage 1; stage 2 transfers Manson's surplus (210), electing Macdonald with a final tally of
# 379.03609 -- see ScottishRealElectionFixtureTest for the round-by-round spot-checks.
